cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Anvil, please cite it as below."
title: "Anvil: an executable benchmark for LLM-generated HPC operational artifacts"
abstract: >-
  Anvil measures whether the SLURM job scripts an LLM writes for a supercomputer
  are correct, verifying them by submission, execution and effective resource fit
  rather than by textual similarity.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rotundo
    given-names: Antonio
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/antoniorotundo2/anvil"
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - high-performance computing
  - large language models
  - execution-based evaluation
  - SLURM
